---
description: iGovPath project rules (full version in AGENTS.md)
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow `AGENTS.md` at the repo root; it wins over this file. Work through the goals in `PLAN.md` §12 in order, and tick a goal only after running its "done when" checks.

Non-negotiable rules:
- Sample public data only; no real applicant data or ID numbers; never send non-sample data to an LLM.
- AI never ranks, scores, shortlists or rejects applicants (POPIA s71); never show "eligible" or a score about a person.
- AI proposes, an officer approves; nothing AI-made reaches applicants unapproved.
- Never invent dates, offices, salaries, reference numbers or documents; use null and "not stated in the advert". Every extracted field has an evidence quote checked against the source.
- Validate every LLM output with Pydantic (Python) or Zod (TypeScript).
- Public repo: secrets only in `.env`; update `.env.example` for new variables.
- Server-side role checks; officers only act on their own department; `/admin` is admin only.
- Every change writes an `audit_log` row.
